feflow 0.2.1, two fixes. Apply with: patch -p1 -d <site-packages> < feflow-0.2.1.patch

1. feflow/protocols/nonequilibrium_cycling.py: the handle_alchemical_waters call
   passed the solvent component where openfe's helper expects the OpenMM force
   field (system_generator.forcefield). Any point mutation that changes net
   charge (alchemical waters), such as K44A, failed in that call. Passing the
   force field fixes it.
2. feflow/utils/hybrid_topology.py: HybridTopologyFactory._find_exception scanned
   every exception of the force on every lookup, which is quadratic in system
   size. It now looks the unordered atom pair up in a dict built once per force
   (same signature, same return value: the parameter list, or []).

Measured effect: the HyHEL-10 hybrid build went from over 40 min to 4.4 min; the
test fixture from 196 s to 14 s. The system XML is identical except the
barostat's random seed.

feflow main had neither fix on 2026-11-21.

